.TH QFW-TEARDOWN 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Commands"
.SH NAME
qfw-teardown \- release one QFw application runtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-teardown
.RI [ --run-dir " directory" ]
.RI [ --keep-run-dir ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-teardown
reads the application runtime created by
.BR qfw-setup (1),
stops recorded application-owned QPM managers in reverse order, stops the
application-owned directory manager, clears the current-run marker, and removes
the application run directory.
.PP
Site-owned directory services, DVMs, and QPMs are outside this ownership
boundary and are never stopped by application teardown. Legacy application
process records remain supported for runtimes created by older launch paths.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --run-dir " directory"
Tear down an explicit application runtime. Without this option, the current
runtime is selected.
.TP
.B --keep-run-dir
Keep generated state and logs after stopping application-owned services and
clearing the current-run marker.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates that all application-owned components stopped successfully.
Incomplete cleanup or unreadable runtime state returns nonzero.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-setup (1),
.BR qfw-status (1),
.BR qfw-srun (1),
.BR qfw-deactivate (1),
.BR qfw-service-plane (7),
.BR qfw (7)
